---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "@/components/dumb/Hero.astro";
import NumberedSection from "@/components/dumb/NumberedSection.astro";
import WorkLog from "@/components/dumb/WorkLog.astro";
import NowSection from "@/components/dumb/NowSection.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <Hero>
        <Fragment slot="lede">
            I build, break and occasionally fix systems on the open web —
            full-stack, infrastructure, the slightly haunted parts in between.
            Currently shipping software at <a
                href="https://gokstadakademiet.no/?ref=bjornar.dev"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener">Gokstad Akademiet</a
            >, and quietly maintaining <a
                href="https://nuva.no/?ref=bjornar.dev"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener">NUVA</a
            >.
        </Fragment>
    </Hero>

    <NumberedSection num="01" title="Personal" sub="// who is HB">
        <p>
            Born and raised in Larvik, Norway. Currently living in Sandefjord.
        </p>
        <p>
            I&rsquo;ve always loved building and taking things apart, so when
            I at a young age was introduced to computers, it didn&rsquo;t take
            very long before I was taking them apart and learning about how
            they worked. When I was 14 I saved up scholarship money originally
            meant for school equipment to instead buy computer parts so I
            could build my first desktop computer. Once I had that built, I
            started learning about code and software. I was instantly
            fascinated with the web technologies and building websites. Since
            then I&rsquo;ve learnt more and more about programming and
            different software technologies.
        </p>
    </NumberedSection>

    <NumberedSection num="02" title="Career" sub="// 14 years &amp; counting">
        <p>
            I learnt HTML, CSS, JS and PHP through self study and got a few
            gigs through some close friends. Later on I got my first
            &ldquo;real job&rdquo; as an apprentice at Optimale Systemer in
            Larvik. Around the same time I started the company Datahjelpen so
            to take on extra jobs outside of work and school.
        </p>
        <p>
            After 2 years at Optimale Systemer I had learned a lot and
            considered myself a full-stack web developer, though still very
            much a junior. I now knew how to setup the LEMP stack from scratch
            on a VPS, and I could make both the front-end and back-end of a
            webapp. After this I moved to Halden to start on my Bachelor of
            Science in Computer Engineering at &Oslash;stfold College
            University.
        </p>
        <p>
            3 years later I got my degree and moved to Sandefjord, where I
            still live. I started working full-time in Datahjelpen. After a
            good year, Covid unfortunately became a thing. I had to find a
            more stable job as no one was willing to start new projects at the
            time. That is how I ended up at Adstate, where I stayed for 4
            years.
        </p>
        <p>
            In 2023 I started <a
                href="https://nuva.no/?ref=bjornar.dev"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener">NUVA</a
            > with a couple of friends.
        </p>
        <p>
            I&rsquo;m currently working full-time at <a
                href="https://gokstadakademiet.no/?ref=bjornar.dev"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener">Gokstad Akademiet</a
            >.
        </p>
    </NumberedSection>

    <WorkLog />

    <NowSection />
</Layout>
